<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title>10.3 Embeddings and Vector Stores — AI Practitioner Associate</title><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght,SOFT@0,9..144,300..800,0..100;1,9..144,300..800,0..100&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&family=DM+Sans:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..40,400..700;1,9..40,400..700&display=swapfamily=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght,SOFT@0,9..144,300..800,0..100;1,9..144,300..800,0..100&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&family=DM+Sans:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..40,400..700;1,9..40,400..700&display=swapfamily=DM+Sans:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..40,400..700;1,9..40,400..700https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght,SOFT@0,9..144,300..800,0..100;1,9..144,300..800,0..100&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&family=DM+Sans:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..40,400..700;1,9..40,400..700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/course-styles.css"></head><body><div class="progress-circle-wrap"><svg viewBox="0 0 36 36"><circle class="progress-circle-track" cx="18" cy="18" r="15"/><circle class="progress-circle-fill" cx="18" cy="18" r="15" id="progressCircle"/></svg><div class="progress-circle-label" id="progressLabel">0%</div></div><nav class="topnav"><div class="topnav-inner"><a href="https://sustainsys.co.uk" class="nav-logo"><img src="../../assets/logo_only.png" alt="SustainSys" class="nav-logo-img"><div class="nav-logo-text">Sustain<span>Sys</span></div></a><div class="nav-divider"></div><div class="nav-title">Module 10 — Embeddings and Vectors</div><span class="nav-badge">Associate</span><a href="index.html" class="nav-home-link">← Course Home</a></div></nav><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sidebar-course-title">AI Practitioner Associate</div><span class="sidebar-section-label">Module 10: RAG Pipelines</span><ul class="sidebar-nav"><li><a href="../learn.html?c=associate&l=module10-lesson1"><span class="sidebar-num">10.1</span> What is RAG?</a></li><li><a href="../learn.html?c=associate&l=module10-lesson2"><span class="sidebar-num">10.2</span> Document Chunking</a></li><li><a href="../learn.html?c=associate&l=module10-lesson3" class="active"><span class="sidebar-num">10.3</span> Embeddings &amp; Vectors</a></li><li><a href="../learn.html?c=associate&l=module10-lesson4"><span class="sidebar-num">10.4</span> Building RAG</a></li><li><a href="../learn.html?c=associate&l=module10-lesson5"><span class="sidebar-num">10.5</span> RAG Evaluation</a></li></ul></aside><button class="sidebar-toggle">☰</button><main class="main"><div class="container"><section class="hero"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Associate</a><span class="sep">›</span><span>Embeddings and Vectors</span></div><span class="hero-eyebrow">Module 10 · Lesson 3</span><h1>Embeddings and Vector Stores</h1><p class="hero-sub">Learn how to convert text into numerical vectors that capture semantic meaning. Understand embedding models, vector databases, and similarity search. Master the retrieval mechanism that powers RAG systems and enables finding relevant documents instantly from millions of options.</p></section><div class="objectives"><h4>Learning Objectives</h4><ul><li>Understand how embeddings convert text to numbers while preserving meaning</li><li>Know the difference between word embeddings, sentence embeddings, and dense passage retrieval</li><li>Compare embedding models: OpenAI, open-source, specialized models</li><li>Implement embedding generation using LangChain and OpenAI</li><li>Understand vector databases and how they store and index embeddings</li><li>Implement similarity search for document retrieval</li><li>Optimize embedding choice for your specific domain</li><li>Handle scaling challenges with large document collections</li></ul></div><section class="section" id="embedding-fundamentals"><span class="section-label">Fundamentals</span><h2>What Are Embeddings?</h2><p>Embeddings are dense numerical vectors that represent text in a way that captures semantic meaning. Instead of storing text as strings, embeddings convert text into points in high-dimensional space where similar content is close together and dissimilar content is far apart. This geometric property enables retrieval: find the embedding closest to your query and you've found the most semantically similar document.</p><p>The power of embeddings is remarkable: with just a few hundred numbers, you can capture complex semantic meaning. A query about "return policies" maps to the same region as documents about "refund procedures" even though they use different words. This semantic similarity—not keyword matching—is what enables effective RAG retrieval.</p><div class="key-concept"><strong>Core Insight:</strong> Embeddings solve the vocabulary problem. Different people use different words for the same concept. Embeddings capture meaning beyond surface-level text, enabling retrieval based on intent rather than keywords.</div><svg viewBox="0 0 800 300" style="width:100%; max-width:700px; margin:20px auto; display:block;"><defs><marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="9" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#333"/></marker></defs><g><rect x="20" y="40" width="120" height="80" fill="#e8f4f8" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2" rx="4"/><text x="80" y="75" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Text</text><text x="80" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">"refund policy"</text><path d="M 140 80 L 200 80" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/><rect x="200" y="40" width="120" height="80" fill="#fff4e6" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2" rx="4"/><text x="260" y="75" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Embedding Model</text><text x="260" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">Convert to vector</text><path d="M 320 80 L 380 80" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/><rect x="380" y="40" width="120" height="80" fill="#e8f8e8" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2" rx="4"/><text x="440" y="70" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Vector</text><text x="440" y="90" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">[0.12, -0.45,</text><text x="440" y="105" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">0.78, ..., 0.34]</text><circle cx="640" cy="80" r="50" fill="#f4e8f8" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2"/><text x="640" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Vector Space</text><text x="640" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">Similarity search</text><text x="400" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold">Embedding Pipeline</text></g></svg></section><section class="section" id="embedding-models"><span class="section-label">Models</span><h2>Choosing and Using Embedding Models</h2><p>Different embedding models have different strengths. Choice affects retrieval quality, cost, and latency. Popular options include OpenAI embeddings (state-of-the-art but proprietary), open-source models like Sentence Transformers (free, can run locally), and specialized models for specific domains.</p><div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Generate embeddings with OpenAI</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">langchain.embeddings.openai</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">OpenAIEmbeddings</span>

<span class="va">embeddings</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAIEmbeddings</span>(<span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"text-embedding-3-small"</span>)

<span class="cm"># Embed a single text</span>
<span class="va">query_embedding</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">embeddings</span>.<span class="fn">embed_query</span>(<span class="st">"What is the return policy?"</span>)
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Vector dimension: {len(query_embedding)}"</span>)

<span class="cm"># Embed multiple documents</span>
<span class="va">documents</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="st">"Refund policy details..."</span>, <span class="st">"Return shipping info..."</span>]
<span class="va">doc_embeddings</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">embeddings</span>.<span class="fn">embed_documents</span>(<span class="va">documents</span>)</code></pre><div class="subsection"><h3>OpenAI Embeddings</h3><p>State-of-the-art performance. text-embedding-3-small is efficient and cost-effective. text-embedding-3-large for maximum quality. Dimensions: 512 (small) to 3072 (large). Costs scale with usage. Best for most production RAG systems.</p></div><div class="subsection"><h3>Open-Source Models</h3><p>Run locally for free. Sentence Transformers library provides many options. Good for privacy-sensitive applications. Slightly lower quality than proprietary models. Hundreds of specialized models available for different domains.</p><div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Open-source embeddings with Sentence Transformers</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">langchain.embeddings</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">HuggingFaceEmbeddings</span>

<span class="va">embeddings</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">HuggingFaceEmbeddings</span>(
    <span class="va">model_name</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"</span>
)

<span class="va">query_vec</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">embeddings</span>.<span class="fn">embed_query</span>(<span class="st">"return policy"</span>)
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Embedding size: {len(query_vec)}"</span>)</code></pre></div></section><section class="section" id="vector-stores"><span class="section-label">Implementation</span><h2>Vector Databases and Retrieval</h2><p>Vector databases store embeddings with efficient similarity search. Unlike traditional databases that find exact matches, vector databases find approximate nearest neighbors—the most similar embeddings to your query. This enables retrieval from millions of documents in milliseconds.</p><div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Store documents in vector database</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">langchain.vectorstores</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">Chroma</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">langchain.embeddings.openai</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">OpenAIEmbeddings</span>

<span class="va">embeddings</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAIEmbeddings</span>()

<span class="cm"># Create vector store from documents</span>
<span class="va">vector_store</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">Chroma</span>.<span class="fn">from_documents</span>(
    <span class="va">documents</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">chunks</span>,
    <span class="va">embedding</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">embeddings</span>,
    <span class="va">persist_directory</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"./vector_db"</span>
)

<span class="cm"># Similarity search</span>
<span class="va">query</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"How do I return items?"</span>
<span class="va">results</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">vector_store</span>.<span class="fn">similarity_search</span>(<span class="va">query</span>, <span class="va">k</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">5</span>)
<span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">result</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">results</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="va">result</span>.<span class="fn">page_content</span>)</code></pre><div class="subsection"><h3>Popular Vector Databases</h3><p><strong>Chroma:</strong> Open-source, local, easy to use. Great for development and small deployments. No infrastructure to manage.</p><p><strong>Pinecone:</strong> Fully managed cloud service. Massive scale (billions of vectors). Easy to use but requires API keys and monthly fees.</p><p><strong>Milvus:</strong> Open-source, scalable. Self-hosted deployment. Good balance of features and control. Requires infrastructure.</p><p><strong>Weaviate:</strong> Open-source, cloud-native. Supports various embedding models natively. GraphQL API. Good for complex queries.</p></div></section><section class="section" id="similarity-metrics"><span class="section-label">Advanced</span><h2>Similarity Metrics and Distance Calculations</h2><p>Vector databases use distance metrics to find similar embeddings. Most common: cosine similarity (compares angles) and Euclidean distance (actual distance). Choice affects retrieval quality and performance.</p><div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Similarity search with different metrics</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">sklearn.metrics.pairwise</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">cosine_similarity</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">numpy</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="im">np</span>

<span class="cm"># Query and document embeddings</span>
<span class="va">query_vec</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([[<span class="nm">0.1</span>, <span class="nm">0.5</span>, <span class="nm">0.3</span>]])
<span class="va">doc_vec</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([[<span class="nm">0.15</span>, <span class="nm">0.48</span>, <span class="nm">0.32</span>]])

<span class="cm"># Cosine similarity (angle between vectors)</span>
<span class="va">similarity</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">cosine_similarity</span>(<span class="va">query_vec</span>, <span class="va">doc_vec</span>)[<span class="nm">0</span>][<span class="nm">0</span>]
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Cosine similarity: {similarity:.4f}"</span>)

<span class="cm"># Euclidean distance</span>
<span class="va">distance</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">linalg</span>.<span class="fn">norm</span>(<span class="va">query_vec</span> <span class="op">-</span> <span class="va">doc_vec</span>)
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Euclidean distance: {distance:.4f}"</span>)</code></pre><p><strong>Cosine Similarity:</strong> Range 0-1. Higher is more similar. Best for high-dimensional sparse data. Most common for embeddings.</p><p><strong>Euclidean Distance:</strong> Actual geometric distance. Sensitive to magnitude. Good when vector magnitude matters.</p></section><section class="section" id="scaling"><span class="section-label">Production</span><h2>Scaling Vector Storage and Production Considerations</h2><p>As document collections grow from thousands to millions, vector storage scaling becomes critical. Production systems must balance accuracy, latency, and cost.</p><h3>Scaling Strategies</h3><ul><li><strong>Index Type:</strong> ANN (Approximate Nearest Neighbor) indexes like HNSW enable fast search on large collections. Trade small accuracy loss for 100x speed improvement.</li><li><strong>Dimensionality Reduction:</strong> Higher dimensions (3072) more accurate but slower. Lower dimensions (384) faster but less precise. Test trade-offs on your data.</li><li><strong>Batch Operations:</strong> Batch embedding and storage for efficiency with large datasets. Embed 100 documents at once, not one by one.</li><li><strong>Quantization:</strong> Reduce vector precision (float32 to uint8) for smaller memory footprint. Save 4x memory with minimal quality loss.</li><li><strong>Caching:</strong> Cache common queries' embedding and results. Avoid re-embedding the same question twice.</li></ul><h3>Performance Optimization Example</h3><div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Batch embedding for efficiency</span>
<span class="va">documents</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="st">"doc1..."</span>, <span class="st">"doc2..."</span>, <span class="st">"doc3..."</span>]  <span class="cm"># 1000+ docs</span>

<span class="cm"># Batch size 100 is much faster than size 1</span>
<span class="va">batch_size</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">100</span>
<span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">i</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="fn">range</span>(<span class="nm">0</span>, <span class="fn">len</span>(<span class="va">documents</span>), <span class="va">batch_size</span>):
    <span class="va">batch</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">documents</span>[<span class="va">i</span>:<span class="va">i</span><span class="op">+</span><span class="va">batch_size</span>]
    <span class="va">embeddings</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">embedding_model</span>.<span class="fn">embed_documents</span>(<span class="va">batch</span>)
    <span class="cm"># Store batch in vector database</span>

<span class="cm"># Monitor and tune performance</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">time</span>
<span class="va">start</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>()
<span class="va">results</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">vector_store</span>.<span class="fn">similarity_search</span>(<span class="st">"query"</span>, <span class="va">k</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">5</span>)
<span class="va">latency</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>() <span class="op">-</span> <span class="va">start</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Query latency: {latency * 1000:.2f}ms"</span>)</code></pre><h3>Cost Optimization</h3><p>Embedding API calls are expensive at scale. Strategies to reduce costs: (1) Use cheaper open-source embeddings where quality is acceptable. (2) Cache embeddings—never embed the same text twice. (3) Batch requests to reduce API overhead. (4) Only embed new documents when knowledge base updates. (5) Monitor embedding quality vs. cost trade-offs.</p></section><section class="section" id="hybrid-search"><span class="section-label">Advanced Patterns</span><h2>Hybrid Search and Re-ranking</h2><p>Pure semantic search misses keyword matches. Hybrid approaches combine semantic and keyword search for better coverage.</p><div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Hybrid search: semantic + keyword</span>
<span class="cm"># Combine BM25 (keyword) and vector (semantic) search</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">langchain.retrievers</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">BM25Retriever</span>, <span class="fn">EnsembleRetriever</span>

<span class="cm"># BM25 retriever (keyword-based)</span>
<span class="va">bm25_retriever</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">BM25Retriever</span>.<span class="fn">from_documents</span>(<span class="va">documents</span>)

<span class="cm"># Vector retriever (semantic)</span>
<span class="va">vector_retriever</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">vector_store</span>.<span class="fn">as_retriever</span>()

<span class="cm"># Combine: take top results from both</span>
<span class="va">ensemble_retriever</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">EnsembleRetriever</span>(
    <span class="va">retrievers</span><span class="op">=</span>[<span class="va">bm25_retriever</span>, <span class="va">vector_retriever</span>],
    <span class="va">weights</span><span class="op">=</span>[<span class="nm">0.5</span>, <span class="nm">0.5</span>]  <span class="cm"># Equal weight to both</span>
)

<span class="va">hybrid_results</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">ensemble_retriever</span>.<span class="fn">get_relevant_documents</span>(<span class="st">"query"</span>)</code></pre></section><section class="section" id="summary"><span class="section-label">Summary</span><h2>Key Takeaways</h2><ul><li><strong>Embeddings:</strong> Dense vectors capturing semantic meaning. Similar content has similar vectors.</li><li><strong>Embedding Models:</strong> OpenAI for best quality, open-source for privacy and cost.</li><li><strong>Vector Databases:</strong> Enable similarity search in milliseconds. Different options for different scales.</li><li><strong>Retrieval Quality:</strong> Depends on embedding model quality, document chunking, and similarity metric choice.</li><li><strong>Scaling:</strong> Use efficient indexes (HNSW) and lower dimensions for very large collections.</li></ul></div><section class="section" id="embeddings-domain"><span class="section-label">Advanced</span><h2>Domain-Specific Embedding Models</h2><p>Different domains require different embeddings. General-purpose embeddings work everywhere but specialized embeddings excel in specific domains. Choose embeddings based on your content and task.</p><h3>Domain Embeddings for RAG</h3><p><strong>Legal Documents:</strong> Use embeddings trained on legal text. They understand terminology like "plaintiff," "jurisdiction," "liability." General embeddings confuse legal jargon.</p><p><strong>Medical/Life Sciences:</strong> Medical terminology differs vastly from general English. Medical embeddings understand "hypertension" as related to "blood pressure," not just word similarity.</p><p><strong>Financial Services:</strong> Financial embeddings capture domain concepts: "APR" relates to "interest rate," "basis points," "yield." Financial institutions often train proprietary embeddings.</p><p><strong>E-commerce:</strong> Product embeddings capture semantic similarity: "men's running shoes" should be similar to "athletic footwear for men." General embeddings might cluster by word overlap instead.</p><h3>Selecting and Evaluating Embeddings</h3><div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Test different embedding models on your domain</span>
<span class="cm"># Evaluate: quality, speed, cost, and domain fit</span>

<span class="va">embedding_candidates</span> <span class="op">=</span> {
    <span class="st">"openai"</span>: <span class="fn">OpenAIEmbeddings</span>(<span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"text-embedding-3-large"</span>),
    <span class="st">"bge-large"</span>: <span class="fn">HuggingFaceEmbeddings</span>(<span class="va">model_name</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5"</span>),
    <span class="st">"legal-bert"</span>: <span class="fn">HuggingFaceEmbeddings</span>(<span class="va">model_name</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"zlucia/custom-legalbert"</span>),
}

<span class="cm"># Benchmark on your test queries</span>
<span class="va">test_queries</span> <span class="op">=</span> [
    <span class="st">"return policy for defective items"</span>,
    <span class="st">"how to request a refund"</span>,
    <span class="st">"shipping duration to Europe"</span>,
]

<span class="va">results</span> <span class="op">=</span> {}
<span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">model_name</span>, <span class="va">embedding_model</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">embedding_candidates</span>.<span class="fn">items</span>():
    <span class="va">vector_store</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">Chroma</span>.<span class="fn">from_documents</span>(
        <span class="va">documents</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">chunks</span>,
        <span class="va">embedding</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">embedding_model</span>
    )

    <span class="va">quality_score</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">0</span>
    <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">query</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">test_queries</span>:
        <span class="va">results_list</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">vector_store</span>.<span class="fn">similarity_search</span>(<span class="va">query</span>, <span class="va">k</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">1</span>)
        <span class="cm"># Manually score: is top result relevant?</span>
        <span class="va">quality_score</span> <span class="op">+=</span> <span class="nm">1</span> <span class="cm"># If relevant (subjective)</span>

    <span class="va">results</span>[<span class="va">model_name</span>] <span class="op">=</span> {
        <span class="st">"quality"</span>: <span class="va">quality_score</span> <span class="op">/</span> <span class="fn">len</span>(<span class="va">test_queries</span>),
        <span class="st">"speed"</span>: <span class="st">"measure embedding time"</span>,
        <span class="st">"cost"</span>: <span class="st">"compare API costs"</span>
    }

<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"Embedding model comparison:"</span>)
<span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">model_name</span>, <span class="va">metrics</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">results</span>.<span class="fn">items</span>():
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"  {model_name}: quality={metrics['quality']:.0%}"</span>)</code></pre></section><div class="exercise-box"><h3>Exercise: Embedding Similarity and Comparison</h3><ol><li>Generate embeddings for 10 policy documents using two different models</li><li>Generate embeddings for 5 customer questions using both models</li><li>Manually examine similarity scores between questions and documents for each model</li><li>Do the highest-scoring matches feel semantically correct?</li><li>Which model retrieves more relevant results for your domain?</li><li>Compare embedding quality vs. cost vs. speed for your use case</li></ol></div><div class="nav-buttons"><a href="../learn.html?c=associate&l=module10-lesson2" class="nav-btn prev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M15 18l-6-6 6-6"/></svg> Previous</a><a href="../learn.html?c=associate&l=module10-lesson4" class="nav-btn next">Next <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></div></div></main><footer><div class="container"><div class="footer-logo"><img src="../../assets/logo_only.png" alt="SustainSys" class="footer-logo-img"><div class="footer-logo-text">Sustain<span>Sys</span> AI Academy</div></div><p>© 2026 SustainSys.</p><p><a href="https://sustainsys.co.uk">sustainsys.co.uk</a></p></div></footer><script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@supabase/supabase-js@2/dist/umd/supabase.min.js"></script>
